From d3caa17dc55f049900509d278ccbbb11155c6c9a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 06:06:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): do not hold active_pr on another card's pull
 [daveey]

Ported from PR212 (7d7c542ce76) onto current main. Among this card's own or
unknown-provenance publication comments (known foreign-writer comments are
already FYI), a pull that is another live card's completion_contract, or
that is named only to say it does not block this card, is not duplicate-PR
evidence. This card's own completion_contract still holds. Only comments
that keep a holding pull order the latest_pr_comment_id watermark; FYI
queue-rejection notes are unchanged. The policy lives in
kanban_db_dispatch_pr_policy.

The hold notice reads checks with the same gh argv as pr_state (broker
prefix), reports "0 failing checks" when the read succeeded with none and
"failing checks unavailable" only when unreadable. The fix card no longer
tells a dispatcher worker to unblock or schedule the held card.
---
